@startuml
title Declarative physical database registration

skinparam sequenceFontSize 14

participant "Kubernetes API" as K8s
participant "DBaaS Operator" as Operator
participant "DBaaS Adapter" as Adapter
participant "DBaaS Aggregator" as Aggregator
database "Registry" as Registry

K8s -> Operator: reconcile PhysicalDatabase\n(created, spec changed, refresh annotation,\nsibling changed, periodic re-sync)

opt spec.operatorNamespace belongs to another operator
  Operator --> K8s: skip the resource, write no status
end

opt another CR claims the same spec.adapterAddress
  Operator --> K8s: InvalidConfiguration, Stalled=True\nReason=RegistrationConflict
end

Operator -> K8s: read the credentials Secret
opt the Secret is absent, a key is missing, or RBAC denies the read
  Operator --> K8s: BackingOff, Reason=SecretError
end

Operator -> Adapter: probe\nGET {adapterAddress}/api/v2/adapter/physical_database\n(Basic Auth from the Secret)
Adapter --> Operator: 200: physicalDatabaseId, type, supportedRoles,\nfeatures, labels, readOnlyHost, apiVersions
opt the probe answers 401
  Operator --> K8s: BackingOff, Reason=Unauthorized
end
opt the probe answers 404 / 503, is unreachable,\nor answers 200 without a required field
  Operator --> K8s: BackingOff, Reason=AdapterError
end

Operator -> K8s: copy the answer into the status

opt another CR reports the same status.physicalDatabaseId
  Operator --> K8s: InvalidConfiguration, Stalled=True\nReason=RegistrationConflict
end

Operator -> Aggregator: register\nPUT /api/v3/dbaas/{type}/physical_databases/{phydbid}?internalMigration=true\n(spec: adapterAddress, Secret: credentials, probe: the rest,\nfixed: status="running", apiVersion="v2")

alt the address or the identifier conflicts with the stored registration
  Aggregator --> Operator: 409 Conflict\nCORE-DBAAS-4057 (address) / CORE-DBAAS-4011 (identifier)
  Operator --> K8s: InvalidConfiguration, Stalled=True\nReason=AggregatorRejected
else the physical database is not registered
  Aggregator -> Registry: save the physical database\n(roles lowercased, password encrypted,\nthe first database of the type is flagged global)
  Aggregator --> Operator: 201 Created
  Operator --> K8s: Succeeded, Ready=True\nReason=PhysicalDatabaseRegistered
else the registration is locked by a running migration
  Aggregator --> Operator: 202 Accepted
  Operator --> K8s: WaitingForDependency, Ready=False\nReason=RoleMigrationStarted
else a role migration is required
  Aggregator -> Registry: create or reuse the instruction\n(the parked registration request)
  opt the instruction carries stored failures
    Aggregator --> Operator: 500 with the stored failures\n(the migration restarts)
    Operator --> K8s: BackingOff, Reason=AggregatorError
  end
  Aggregator --> Operator: 202 Accepted
  note right of Aggregator: the internal migration runs;\nsee Internal role migration
  Operator --> K8s: WaitingForDependency, Ready=False\nReason=RoleMigrationStarted
else no migration is required
  Aggregator -> Registry: update the row when a property differs,\nreset the caches
  Aggregator --> Operator: 200 OK
  Operator --> K8s: Succeeded, Ready=True\nReason=PhysicalDatabaseRegistered
end

note over Operator
  On 202 the operator does not read the body.
  It repeats the registration with the poll backoff
  (5 s doubling to 1 min) until the aggregator answers 200.
end note
@enduml
